-- 197b CHOP AND SCREW — the ending of the 197 SOARING take, as a self-escalating scene.
-- @scene {"title":"Chop and Screw","cps":0.6875,"quantize":1}
--
-- WHERE THIS CAME FROM
--   recordings/197-soaring-take-20261114-1544.flac (+ .wav, .markers.jsonl)
--   A ~6 minute improvised take through three breakdowns, ending in a chop/screw
--   disintegration. This file reproduces the ENDING so it can be jumped into
--   directly instead of rebuilt by hand.
--
-- WHAT MADE THE ENDING WORK (worth not losing)
--   1. THE LEAD IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT. Every other lane survived the
--      destruction; the piano lead did not. Dropping it is what left room for
--      the break to be mangled - with the lead on top the chaos read as noise,
--      without it the grinding reads as texture. Do not add a melody back.
--   2. DESTRUCTION IS A RAMP, NOT A SWITCH. speed falls 1.4 -> 0.1, crush
--      16 -> 1, lpf 14k -> 300 Hz, delay feedback 0.35 -> 0.9, each in 8 stages
--      of 8 bars over 64 bars (~93 s at 165 BPM). Every stage is audible as its
--      own thing, so it escalates rather than just becoming loud mush.
--   3. stutWith CARRIES THE DENSITY. The stutter is what turns the breakdown
--      into a smear: it is on the LIST, not on the break, so the grain comes
--      from repetition rather than from the source.
--
--   WARNING - EVENT DENSITY, MEASURED. The live take ran
--     stutWith 32 $ chop 64 $ slice 16   = 32,768 events/cycle
--   which is an OSC flood, not a musical stutter; SuperDirt silently drops most
--   of it, so what you hear is not what the pattern says. Measured sizes:
--     chop64 + slice16            -> 1024/cycle
--     chop64 + slice16 + stut8    -> 8192/cycle   (still a flood)
--     chop16 + slice8  + stut4    ->  512/cycle   <- this file uses this
--   When something sounds impossibly dense, count events per cycle before
--   believing it: `length (queryArc p (Arc 0 1))`.
--   4. THE RHODES GETS SCREWED SEPARATELY, on its own slower ramp (slow 4 and a
--      1.4 -> 0.3 speed drop), so chords and break disintegrate at different
--      rates and never line up into a single pull-down.
--
-- HOW TO USE IT
--   Play it as-is for the full 93 s ascent, or jump straight to a stage by
--   cropping the <...> values (e.g. start at "0.35 0.2 0.1" for the last third).
--   To end from here, hush - the take ended with a hard stop, which is the
--   intended ending.
--
-- TEMPO 165, same as 197-soaring.tidal, so the two can chase each other.
-- MIXING STANDARD  written for ~masterBootGain = 5. No amp: gain only.

setcps (165/60/4)

-- THE BREAK, DISINTEGRATING. stutWith 32 at 1/128 supplies the grain; chop 64
-- and a rotating slice order supply the wrongness. speed/crush/lpf/feedback all
-- ramp on slow 8 over 8 stages.
d1 $ stutWith 4 0.0625 (|* gain 0.4) $ chop 16 $ slice 8 "3 1 4 0 7 2 6 5" $ s "breaks165" # orbit 0 # gain 0.75 # hpf (slow 8 "<120 200 300 400 500 600 700 800>") # lpf (slow 8 "<14000 12000 9000 6000 3800 2000 900 300>") # speed (slow 8 "<1.4 1.2 1.0 0.78 0.6 0.42 0.25 0.12>") # crush (slow 8 "<16 14 12 9 6 4 2 1>") # shape (slow 8 "<0.1 0.2 0.3 0.45 0.6 0.75 0.88 0.95>") # delay (slow 8 "<0.25 0.3 0.35 0.42 0.5 0.58 0.65 0.7>") # delaytime (3/16) # delayfeedback (slow 8 "<0.35 0.4 0.45 0.5 0.6 0.7 0.8 0.9>") # lock 1

-- THE SUB. Deliberately left CLEAN - it is the pitch anchor, and if it screws
-- too the whole thing loses its floor and stops sounding like music at all.
d6 $ slow 2 $ note "a1 ~ ~ ~ a1 ~ ~ ~ e2 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ fs2 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ d2 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~" # s "dubsub" # orbit 5 # gain 0.85 # hpf 28 # lpf 400 # waveMix 0 # subMix 1 # fenv 0 # attack 0.006 # release 1.3 # sustain 0.9 # dry 0.95 # room 0.06

-- THE RHODES, SCREWED ON ITS OWN CLOCK. slow 4 rather than slow 8, and a
-- separate 1.4 -> 0.3 speed fall, so it never disintegrates in step with d1.
d9 $ swingBy 0.14 4 $ slow 4 $ struct "t(3,8,1)" $ n "<3 0 2 0 3 2 0 2>" # s "mars_synths_DrSample_Rhodes_Chords" # speed (slow 4 $ range 1.4 0.3 saw) # orbit 8 # gain 0.6 # hpf (slow 4 $ range 180 600 sine) # lpf (slow 4 $ range 6000 800 saw) # attack 0.004 # release 0.9 # sustain 0.5 # room 0.55 # size 0.92 # dry 0.5 # delay (slow 4 $ range 0.2 0.55 saw) # delaytime (3/16) # delayfeedback (slow 4 $ range 0.35 0.75 saw) # lock 1
